+# VMAF Calculator with MongoDB Auto-Storage
+
+Calculate VMAF scores and automatically store them in MongoDB for tracking video quality across your content library.
+
+## Quick Start
+
+### 1. Install Dependencies
+
+```bash
+cd /Users/cstech-05/Desktop/vmaf/vmaf
+source venv/bin/activate
+pip install pymongo dnspython
+```
+
+### 2. Run VMAF with MongoDB Storage
+
+```bash
+python run_vmaf.py \
+  -r /path/to/reference_video.mp4 \
+  -d /path/to/transcoded_video.mp4 \
+  --show-id "show_001" \
+  --show-title "Breaking Bad" \
+  --episode 1 \
+  --trail-name "1080p_high"
+```
+
+That's it! The VMAF score will be automatically calculated and stored in MongoDB.
+
+## Features
+
+✅ **Automatic MongoDB Storage** - Every VMAF calculation is saved to MongoDB
+✅ **Unique Constraint** - Prevents duplicate records (show_id + episode + trail + resolution)
+✅ **Indexed Collections** - Fast queries by show, episode, or VMAF score
+✅ **Rich Metadata** - Store S3 links, bitrate, resolution, and more
+✅ **Batch Processing** - Process multiple videos with MongoDB storage
+
+## Usage Examples
+
+### Basic Usage
+
+```bash
+# Calculate VMAF and store to MongoDB
+python run_vmaf.py \
+  -r original.mp4 \
+  -d transcoded.mp4 \
+  --show-id "bb_001" \
+  --show-title "Breaking Bad" \
+  --episode 1 \
+  --trail-name "1080p_high"
+```
+
+### With S3 Link
+
+```bash
+# Include S3 link in metadata
+python run_vmaf.py \
+  -r original.mp4 \
+  -d transcoded.mp4 \
+  --s3-link "s3://chai-shots-videos/shows/breaking-bad/s01e01.mp4" \
+  --show-id "bb_001" \
+  --show-title "Breaking Bad" \
+  --episode 1 \
+  --trail-name "1080p_high"
+```
+
+### With M3U8 Stream
+
+```bash
+# Compare against HLS stream
+python run_vmaf.py \
+  -r original.mp4 \
+  -d "https://storage.googleapis.com/bucket/video.m3u8" \
+  --show-id "show_001" \
+  --show-title "My Show" \
+  --episode 1 \
+  --trail-name "720p_medium"
+```
+
+### Different VMAF Models
+
+```bash
+# Use phone model (for mobile viewing)
+python run_vmaf.py \
+  -r ref.mp4 \
+  -d dist.mp4 \
+  --model vmaf_phone \
+  --show-id "show_001" \
+  --show-title "My Show" \
+  --episode 1
+
+# Use 4K model (for 4K content)
+python run_vmaf.py \
+  -r ref.mp4 \
+  -d dist.mp4 \
+  --model vmaf_4k \
+  --show-id "show_001" \
+  --show-title "My Show" \
+  --episode 1
+```
+
+### Disable MongoDB (Traditional Usage)
+
+```bash
+# Calculate VMAF without storing to MongoDB
+python run_vmaf.py \
+  -r reference.mp4 \
+  -d distorted.mp4 \
+  --no-mongodb
+```
+
+### Batch Processing
+
+```bash
+# Process multiple videos with MongoDB storage
+python batch_compare.py \
+  --reference-dir ./originals/ \
+  --distorted-dir ./transcoded/ \
+  -o ./results/ \
+  --mongodb-uri "mongodb+srv://..." \
+  --store-to-mongodb
+```
+
+## Configuration
+
+Edit `vmaf_config.py` to change defaults:
+
+```python
+# MongoDB Configuration
+MONGODB_URI = "your-mongodb-uri"
+MONGODB_ENABLED = True  # Enable by default
+
+# Default VMAF model
+DEFAULT_MODEL = "vmaf_phone"
+
+# Default threads (0 = auto)
+DEFAULT_THREADS = 0
+
+# Verbose output
+VERBOSE = False
+```
+
+You can also use environment variables:
+
+```bash
+export MONGODB_URI="mongodb+srv://..."
+export MONGODB_ENABLED="true"
+export VMAF_MODEL="vmaf_phone"
+export VMAF_THREADS="8"
+```
+
+## MongoDB Schema
+
+Data is stored in the `vmaf_scores` collection:
+
+```json
+{
+  "_id": "ObjectId(...)",
+  "s3_link_name": "s3://bucket/video.mp4",
+  "show_title": "Breaking Bad",
+  "episode_number": 1,
+  "show_id": "bb_001",
+  "trail_name": "1080p_high",
+  "trail_bitrate": 5000000,
+  "resolution": "1920x1080",
+  "vmaf_score": 95.8,
+  "created_at": "2026-02-11T18:48:50.000Z",
+  "updated_at": "2026-02-11T18:48:50.000Z"
+}
+```
+
+### Unique Constraint
+
+The collection enforces uniqueness on:
+- `show_id`
+- `episode_number`
+- `trail_name`
+- `resolution`
+
+This prevents duplicate VMAF scores for the same video configuration.
+
+## Querying MongoDB Data
+
+### Using Python
+
+```python
+from mongodb_client import VMAFMongoDBClient
+
+client = VMAFMongoDBClient(MONGODB_URI)
+
+# Get all scores for a show
+scores = client.get_vmaf_scores_by_show("bb_001")
+
+# Get scores for specific episode
+episode_scores = client.get_vmaf_scores_by_episode("bb_001", 1)
+
+# Calculate average VMAF
+avg_vmaf = client.get_average_vmaf_by_resolution("bb_001", "1920x1080")
+
+client.close()
+```
+
+### Using MongoDB Compass or Shell
+
+```javascript
+// Find all scores for a show
+db.vmaf_scores.find({ show_id: "bb_001" })
+
+// Find scores above 90
+db.vmaf_scores.find({ vmaf_score: { $gte: 90 } })
+
+// Average VMAF by resolution
+db.vmaf_scores.aggregate([
+  { $match: { show_id: "bb_001" } },
+  { $group: {
+    _id: "$resolution",
+    avg_vmaf: { $avg: "$vmaf_score" }
+  }}
+])
+
+// Find lowest quality episodes
+db.vmaf_scores.find().sort({ vmaf_score: 1 }).limit(10)
+```
+
+## Command-Line Reference
+
+### Required Arguments
+
+- `-r, --reference` - Path to reference video (original)
+- `-d, --distorted` - Path or URL to distorted video (transcoded)
+
+### MongoDB Metadata (Required for MongoDB storage)
+
+- `--show-id` - Unique show identifier
+- `--show-title` - Human-readable show title
+- `--episode` - Episode number
+- `--trail-name` - Quality trail name (e.g., "1080p_high", "720p_medium")
+- `--s3-link` - S3 link to video (optional, defaults to distorted path)
+
+### Optional Arguments
+
+- `-o, --output` - Output JSON file (default: vmaf_results.json)
+- `-m, --model` - VMAF model: vmaf_v0.6.1, vmaf_4k, vmaf_b, vmaf_phone
+- `-t, --threads` - Number of threads (0 = auto)
+- `-v, --verbose` - Enable verbose output
+- `--no-mongodb` - Disable MongoDB storage
+- `--mongodb-uri` - Custom MongoDB URI
+
+## VMAF Model Selection
+
+| Model | Use Case | Viewing Distance |
+|-------|----------|------------------|
+| `vmaf_v0.6.1` | HD content on TV/laptop | 3H (3x screen height) |
+| `vmaf_4k` | 4K/UHD content | 1.5H |
+| `vmaf_phone` | Mobile phone viewing | Close distance, small screen |
+| `vmaf_b` | Improved accuracy | General purpose |
+
+**Recommendation:** Use `vmaf_phone` for mobile content as it accounts for smaller screens and closer viewing distances.
+
+## Quality Score Interpretation
+
+| VMAF Score | Quality | Description |
+|------------|---------|-------------|
+| 93-100 | Excellent | Virtually indistinguishable from reference |
+| 80-92 | Good | Minor perceptible differences |
+| 70-79 | Fair | Noticeable quality degradation |
+| 50-69 | Poor | Significant quality loss |
+| 0-49 | Bad | Severe quality degradation |
+
+## Workflow Integration
+
+### Example: GCP Video Transcoding Pipeline
+
+```python
+from vmaf_calculator import VMAFCalculator
+
+def process_transcoded_video(
+    original_path: str,
+    transcoded_url: str,
+    show_info: dict
+):
+    """Process a transcoded video and store VMAF to MongoDB"""
+
+    calculator = VMAFCalculator(
+        reference_path=original_path,
+        distorted_path=transcoded_url,
+        model="vmaf_phone",
+        mongodb_uri=MONGODB_URI,
+        mongodb_enabled=True,
+        show_metadata={
+            "s3_link_name": show_info["s3_path"],
+            "show_title": show_info["title"],
+            "episode_number": show_info["episode"],
+            "show_id": show_info["id"],
+            "trail_name": show_info["trail"],
+        }
+    )
+
+    result = calculator.calculate()
+    return result["metrics"]["vmaf"]["score"]
+```
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+### MongoDB Connection Issues
+
+```bash
+# Test MongoDB connection
+python -c "from mongodb_client import VMAFMongoDBClient; \
+  client = VMAFMongoDBClient('your-uri'); \
+  print('✓ Connected'); client.close()"
+```
+
+### Duplicate Key Errors
+
+If you see duplicate key errors, it means you're trying to insert a VMAF score that already exists for that show/episode/trail/resolution combination. Use the `update_vmaf_score()` method instead:
+
+```python
+from mongodb_client import VMAFMongoDBClient
+
+client = VMAFMongoDBClient(MONGODB_URI)
+client.update_vmaf_score(
+    show_id="bb_001",
+    episode_number=1,
+    trail_name="1080p_high",
+    resolution="1920x1080",
+    vmaf_score=96.5  # new score
+)
+```
+
+### Missing Dependencies
+
+```bash
+# Install all dependencies
+pip install -r requirements.txt
+```
+
+## Files Overview
+
+- `run_vmaf.py` - Main script with MongoDB auto-storage
+- `vmaf_config.py` - Configuration file
+- `mongodb_client.py` - MongoDB operations
+- `vmaf_calculator/vmaf_calculator.py` - Core VMAF calculator
+- `vmaf_calculator/batch_compare.py` - Batch processing
+- `example_vmaf_storage.py` - MongoDB examples
+- `example_vmaf_with_mongodb.py` - Integration examples
+
+## Support
+
+For issues or questions:
+1. Check the logs with `--verbose` flag
+2. Review MongoDB indexes with `db.vmaf_scores.getIndexes()`
+3. Test MongoDB connection separately
+
+## License
+
