+# VMAF Calculator - Complete Documentation
+
+## Table of Contents
+1. [What is VMAF?](#what-is-vmaf)
+2. [Project Overview](#project-overview)
+3. [File Structure](#file-structure)
+4. [How It Works - Step by Step](#how-it-works---step-by-step)
+5. [Understanding Each File](#understanding-each-file)
+6. [VMAF Models Explained](#vmaf-models-explained)
+7. [Code Walkthrough](#code-walkthrough)
+8. [Bitrate Analysis Explained](#bitrate-analysis-explained)
+9. [Common Use Cases](#common-use-cases)
+10. [Troubleshooting](#troubleshooting)
+
+---
+
+## What is VMAF?
+
+### Simple Explanation
+VMAF (Video Multi-Method Assessment Fusion) is a tool created by Netflix to measure video quality. Think of it like a "quality score" for videos.
+
+**Analogy:** Imagine you have a beautiful painting (original video). You make a photocopy of it (compressed video). VMAF tells you how similar the photocopy looks compared to the original painting, on a scale of 0 to 100.
+
+### Why Do We Need VMAF?
+When you upload a video to platforms like YouTube, Netflix, or GCP (Google Cloud Platform), they compress the video to save bandwidth. But compression can reduce quality. VMAF helps answer:
+- "How much quality did we lose?"
+- "Is this compression good enough for viewers?"
+- "Can we compress more without viewers noticing?"
+
+### VMAF Score Meaning
+| Score | Quality | What Viewers See |
+|-------|---------|------------------|
+| 93-100 | Excellent | Cannot tell difference from original |
+| 80-92 | Good | Tiny differences, most won't notice |
+| 70-79 | Fair | Some visible quality loss |
+| 50-69 | Poor | Obvious quality problems |
+| 0-49 | Bad | Severely degraded, unwatchable |
+
+---
+
+## Project Overview
+
+### What This Project Does
+This VMAF Calculator compares two videos:
+1. **Reference Video** - The original, high-quality video (e.g., your source MP4)
+2. **Distorted Video** - The compressed/transcoded video (e.g., M3U8 stream from GCP)
+
+It outputs:
+- VMAF quality score
+- Bitrate analysis (how much bandwidth is saved)
+- Recommendations for your use case
+
+### Our Use Case
+```
+Original MP4 → Upload to GCP → GCP transcodes to M3U8 → Viewed on Phone
+```
+We want to know: "Does the M3U8 stream look good enough on phones?"
+
+---
+
+## File Structure
+
+```
+vmaf_calculator/
+│
+├── vmaf_calculator.py      # Main calculator script (command-line tool)
+├── app.py                  # Web server (Flask application)
+├── requirements.txt        # Python dependencies list
+├── setup.sh               # Automatic setup script
+├── batch_compare.py       # Compare multiple videos at once
+├── DOCUMENTATION.md       # This file - explains everything
+├── README.md              # Quick start guide
+│
+├── templates/
+│   └── index.html         # Web interface (what you see in browser)
+│
+├── uploads/               # Where uploaded videos are stored
+├── results/               # Where JSON results are saved
+└── venv/                  # Python virtual environment
+```
+
+### What Each File Does (Simple Explanation)
+
+| File | Purpose | When It's Used |
+|------|---------|----------------|
+| `vmaf_calculator.py` | The brain - does all calculations | When you run from terminal |
+| `app.py` | Web server - handles browser requests | When you use web interface |
+| `index.html` | The face - what users see in browser | When you open localhost:5000 |
+| `requirements.txt` | Shopping list of Python packages | During setup |
+| `setup.sh` | Automatic installer | First time setup |
+| `batch_compare.py` | Bulk processing tool | When comparing many videos |
+
+---
+
+## How It Works - Step by Step
+
+### The Complete Flow
+
+```
+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│                     USER INPUT                                   │
+│  Reference Video (MP4) + Distorted Video (MP4/M3U8)             │
+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+                              │
+                              ▼
+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│                  STEP 1: DOWNLOAD (if M3U8)                     │
+│  If distorted video is M3U8 URL → FFmpeg downloads it           │
+│  M3U8 is a playlist format used for streaming                   │
+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+                              │
+                              ▼
+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│                  STEP 2: ANALYZE VIDEOS                         │
+│  FFprobe extracts info: resolution, fps, bitrate, codec         │
+│  This tells us what we're comparing                             │
+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+                              │
+                              ▼
+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│                  STEP 3: CONVERT TO Y4M                         │
+│  Both videos converted to Y4M format (raw video)                │
+│  Y4M = uncompressed, frame-by-frame format                      │
+│  VMAF tool needs this format to compare pixels                  │
+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+                              │
+                              ▼
+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│                  STEP 4: CALCULATE VMAF                         │
+│  VMAF tool compares each frame:                                 │
+│  - Frame 1 of reference vs Frame 1 of distorted                 │
+│  - Frame 2 of reference vs Frame 2 of distorted                 │
+│  - ... and so on for all frames                                 │
+│  Outputs score for each frame + average score                   │
+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+                              │
+                              ▼
+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│                  STEP 5: APPLY MODEL TRANSFORM                  │
+│  If using phone model → boost scores                            │
+│  (Same video looks better on smaller screens)                   │
+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+                              │
+                              ▼
+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│                  STEP 6: GENERATE REPORT                        │
+│  Calculate bitrate analysis                                     │
