+## VMAF Models Explained
+
+### Why Different Models?
+
+Different viewing situations need different quality measurements:
+
+| Situation | Screen Size | Viewing Distance | Model to Use |
+|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------------|
+| Phone | 6 inches | 1 foot | `vmaf_phone` |
+| Laptop | 15 inches | 2 feet | `vmaf_v0.6.1` |
+| HD TV | 50 inches | 8 feet | `vmaf_v0.6.1` |
+| 4K TV | 65 inches | 6 feet | `vmaf_4k` |
+
+### Model Details
+
+#### 1. vmaf_v0.6.1 (Default)
+- **Trained for:** 1080p HDTV at 3× screen height distance
+- **Use when:** Videos viewed on laptops, regular TVs
+- **Score range:** 0-100 (typically 20-100)
+
+#### 2. vmaf_4k
+- **Trained for:** 4K TV at 1.5× screen height distance
+- **Use when:** Videos viewed on 4K displays
+- **Why different:** 4K viewers sit closer, see more detail
+
+#### 3. vmaf_phone
+- **Based on:** vmaf_v0.6.1 with score transformation
+- **Use when:** Videos viewed on mobile phones
+- **Score difference:** ~10-15 points HIGHER than TV model
+
+**Visual Example:**
+```
+Same compressed video:
+├── TV Model Score:    81.24 (Good)
+└── Phone Model Score: 95.41 (Excellent)
+
+Why? The compression artifacts that are visible on a
+55-inch TV become invisible on a 6-inch phone screen.
+```
+
+#### 4. vmaf_b (v0.6.3)
+- **Improved accuracy** over v0.6.1
+- **Use when:** You need most accurate measurement
+- **Difference:** Slightly better at edge cases
+
+### How Phone Model Transform Works
+
+```python
+def transform_score(vmaf_score):
+    # Formula from Netflix's research
+    p0 = 1.70674692   # Base offset
+    p1 = 1.72643844   # Linear multiplier
+    p2 = -0.00705305  # Quadratic adjustment
+
+    phone_score = p0 + (p1 * vmaf_score) + (p2 * vmaf_score * vmaf_score)
+
+    # Ensure phone score is never LOWER than original
+    phone_score = max(phone_score, vmaf_score)
+
+    # Keep within valid range
+    phone_score = min(max(phone_score, 0), 100)
+
+    return phone_score
+```
+
+**Example calculations:**
+| Original VMAF | Phone VMAF | Boost |
+|---------------|------------|-------|
+| 60 | 78.5 | +18.5 |
+| 70 | 86.7 | +16.7 |
+| 80 | 93.6 | +13.6 |
+| 90 | 99.2 | +9.2 |
