+```
+
+Config file format (`comparisons.json`):
+```json
+{
+  "comparisons": [
+    {"reference": "video1_original.mp4", "distorted": "https://example.com/video1.m3u8", "name": "video1"},
+    {"reference": "video2_original.mp4", "distorted": "video2_transcoded.mp4", "name": "video2"}
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+## VMAF Score Interpretation
+
+| Score Range | Quality |
+|-------------|---------|
+| 93-100 | Excellent - Virtually indistinguishable from reference |
+| 80-92 | Good - Minor perceptible differences |
+| 70-79 | Fair - Noticeable quality degradation |
+| 50-69 | Poor - Significant quality loss |
+| 0-49 | Bad - Severe quality degradation |
+
+## Models
+
+- `vmaf_v0.6.1` (default) - Standard model for HD content
+- `vmaf_4k` - Optimized for 4K/UHD content
+- `vmaf_b` - Improved model with better accuracy
+
+## Output
+
+Results are saved as JSON:
+
+```json
+{
+  "timestamp": "2024-01-15T10:30:00",
+  "reference": {"path": "original.mp4", "info": {...}},
+  "distorted": {"path": "transcoded.m3u8", "info": {...}},
+  "model": "vmaf_v0.6.1",
+  "metrics": {
+    "vmaf": {"score": 92.5, "min": 85.2, "max": 98.1},
+    "psnr": {"y": 42.3, "cb": 45.1, "cr": 44.8},
+    "ssim": 0.9876
+  },
+  "frame_count": 1800
+}
+```
+
+## Requirements
+
+- Python 3.6+
+- FFmpeg with libvmaf support
+- See `requirements.txt` for Python packages
